		(uuid "44b914d1-2de2-5d1f-9a36-885c2d365393")
	)
	(text "Wire colors are the breadboard jumpers in the owner photos\n(2026-09-24), not a harness specification.\nInland 1.3\" OLED V2.0 (KS0056), 4-wire SPI, 3.3 V.\nSH1106 128x64 inferred from the vendor example.\nJ2 pins follow the board header, pin 1 = GND (top).\nGPIO21 (A14, the e-ink BUSY) is unused here."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 175 96.52 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4abc7ffb-abdd-5f94-900e-2cd0ccbf4d9c")
	)
	(text "DECOUPLING"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 175 180 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "56bf73a2-9124-5a61-8197-5cc0a0829ae3")
	)
	(text "BACK / REAR PHOTO VIEW\nJ1 (5V) top-left; A1 (CLK) top-right\nSocket IDs are immutable; this is NOT a footprint view."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 28 21 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "694c6bf1-7687-5c82-ac3e-49dde90b17d9")
	)
	(text "DISPLAY"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 175 40 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "918b9a6a-a89e-5b4a-ba65-5ba264b74363")
	)
	(text "USB-powered DevKit; J1 / 5V feeds only the status ring (J5).\nJ19 supplies +3V3. All three GND sockets connected.\nOnboard USB-UART, regulator, BOOT and EN retained.\nPAIR is the onboard BOOT button (GPIO0, A6): no carrier wiring; A6 stays NC.\nDISPLAY STRAP: A7 (GPIO4) tied to GND = OLED board."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 28 157 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "95b20a59-abd6-5cc6-a5a9-f871e447e7ae")
	)
	(text "C2 10 uF X7R on +3V3; C3 100 nF at U2."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 175 205 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "980356fa-0dc4-5e1a-a04d-af2d300ca6a7")
	)
	(text "gray wire"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 204.47 69.6 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ba739cdf-03b9-5442-a037-4c32ed04cc45")
	)
	(text "SCHEMATIC REVIEW / RELEASE HOLDS\n1. U1 uses A1-A19 / J1-J19 from SigilBackMarked.png (BACK view); never exchange row identities.\n2. U1 footprint (Sigil.pretty): 2.54 mm pitch, rows 22.225 mm (7/8 in, owner measurement 2026-09-28) apart, 25.4 x 53.975 mm outline (1 x 2 1/8 in). Caliper-check and test-fit before ordering.\n3. Future footprint: two 1x19 female sockets, unmistakable A1/J1 marks; verify insertion from carrier component side.\n4. Keep micro-USB, BOOT and EN/reset accessible. U1 carries a 6.35 mm antenna keep-out at the A19/J19 end (measured, 1/4 in).\n5. Footprints: 2.54 mm sockets/headers, JST-XH J5/J6, axial R1/R2, radial C2-C4, SOT-23-5 U2/U3; U1 rows 22.225 mm from the owner measurement: test-fit before ordering.\n6. Discrete LEDs and the old buttons are removed; J4 is the joystick (its \"+5V\" pin MUST be fed 3.3 V); J5 is the Jewel adapter cable on USB 5V.\n7. Rev A is an electrical draft, NOT fabrication-ready until U1 is checked against the real board. Power through DevKit USB; no second supply designed."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 28 211 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bf7fef56-e5db-5d44-b29a-b16aa0063c50")
	)
	(text "J5: JST-XH 3-pin socket for the Jewel adapter pigtail\n(1 +5V, 2 DIN, 3 GND). The Jewel 7 RGBW and its bulk capacitor\nare on Sigil_JewelAdapter. 3.3 V data worked on the breadboard\nbut is below spec, so U2 (74AHCT1G125) buffers GPIO26 to 5 V;\nR1 (330 ohm) at the source damps the cable (the Jewel has its\nown 470 ohm on DIN). Full RGBW is ~560 mA, more than USB\nsupplies: firmware caps brightness at 48/255.\nDraws the status light (LedState); never the only signal."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 290 160.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c9be0766-3d6b-5731-9301-fec4c804f5a4")
	)
	(text "J6: spare front light output, e.g. 6-8 SK6812 RGBW pixels on\nthe case front lip facing the seated player. Own data line:\nGPIO13 -> U3 (74AHCT1G125, C4) -> R2 (330 ohm) -> DIN; pinout as J5.\nShares USB 5V with the ring: firmware must cap both (7 + 8 pixels\nat 48/255 is about 225 mA). Fitted; unused until a strip is added."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 290 226.06 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e2ccc72a-d7b4-5183-b19b-e2d8dbab5f3b")
	)
	(text "Unmarked 5-pin analog thumbstick; pins in module order.\n\"+5V\" pin is fed 3.3 V: VRX/VRY swing to the supply and the\nESP32 ADC must not see 5 V. SW is a switch to GND (internal pull-up).\nDirections + click are the five menu keys (on-screen compass).\nAxis direction depends on mounting; firmware can swap/invert.\nFirmware: Sigil PlatformIO envs sigil and sigil-oled."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 290 86.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e31c32a4-c620-54ad-85a9-0b2f2026cbd4")
	)
	(text "blue wire"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 204.47 79.76 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ed72d4f5-e5d8-5670-b024-bc1879904e5b")
	)
	(text "CONTROLS / JOYSTICK"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 290 40 0)
